>game,T6

// ============================================================================
//  mod_custom_maps.zone - the FRONTEND half of the Custom Maps route.
//
//  Only what the menu needs BEFORE a map is loaded: the map card, its blurred
//  transition copy, the mode card, the signpost pin, the loading-screen
//  materials and the two UI tables the globe and map list read.
//
//  🛑 THE MAP'S GAMEPLAY PAYLOAD IS NOT HERE, AND MUST NEVER COME BACK.
//
//  Octagonal Ascension ships as a standalone mod, so its release mod.ff carries
//  everything the map needs to run: the mystery box, the window barriers, the
//  perk machines, 35 weapons, the Hellhound chain, the player models. That is
//  correct for a mod that only ever loads with its own map. It is fatal here,
//  because zm_qol's mod.ff loads AHEAD OF EVERY STOCK MAP ZONE.
//
//  🔴 v2.17.1 SHIPPED THAT WAY AND ORIGINS WOULD NOT BOOT:
//
//      COM_ERROR: Attempting to override asset 'zmcore_basicwoodbarrier'
//                 from zone 'mod' with zone 'zm_tomb'
//
//  The full unlinked payload was 2,687 assets, and measured against
//  Unlinker --list of zm_transit / zm_prison / zm_buried / zm_tomb /
//  zm_highrise / zm_nuked:
//
//    - 2,299 of them are ALSO owned by a stock map zone. mod.ff loads first,
//      so its copy silently wins on every map - the v1.62.7 Electric Cherry
//      ownership trap (see build_ff.bat), 2,299 assets wide.
//    - 35 are weapons, in a mod with no spare weapon slots.
//    - 12 are of types this mod had never proven overridable, and the engine
//      refused the first one it reached:
//        zbarrier  zmcore_basicwoodbarrier, zmcore_basicwoodbarrier_hide_pieces,
//                  zmcore_magicbox, zmprison_magicbox
//        vehicle   zombie_prison_plane
//        script    _teamset_cdc.gsc/.csc, _zm_melee_weapon.gsc,
//                  _zm_weap_ballistic_knife.gsc, _zm_weap_claymore.gsc,
//                  character_sp_zombie_dog.gsc/.csc
//
//  The payload now lives in zm_octagonal.ff, which only loads when that map
//  loads. See zone_source/octagonal_map/zm_octagonal.zone and
//  zone_ownership_gate.py, which fails the build if any of it comes back.
//
//  Everything below resolves from zone_source\octagonal_donor\mod.ff.
// ============================================================================

// The custom map's own loading picture. No stock zombies fastfile owns this
// name, so it can only add.
image,loadscreen

// 🛑 BOTH TABLES ARE REQUIRED AND BOTH ARE SUPERSETS OF THE RETAIL ROWS.
//  gametypestable.csv carries the start-location entry (section 5) and one row
//  per gametype it is selectable under (section 6); mapstable.csv carries the
//  globe pin. patch_zm owns both and loads BEFORE mod.ff, so overriding them
//  here is the supported direction. A duplicate or missing index in either is a
//  guaranteed COM_ERROR, and a missing globe row is a nil lookup in
//  CoD.GameGlobeZombie.MoveToExpectedMap() on every return to the lobby.
//
//  🛑 THEY ARE STAGED AS REAL CSV IN zone_assets\zm\, NOT RESOLVED FROM A DONOR.
//
//  That is deliberate and both of the obvious alternatives are wrong. The
//  Linker takes a declared asset from the asset search path FIRST and only
//  falls back to a --load'ed fastfile, so staging them settles which rows ship
//  no matter where a donor sits in the load order. Measured, because two
//  different donors offer this name and BOTH are wrong:
//
//    zone_source\octagonal_donor\mod.ff   retail + the zm_octagonal rows, and
//                                         nothing else
//    zone_source\refreshed_donor\mod.ff   Reimagined's own table: 28 start
//                                         locations and its gametype names
//                                         (zsr, zrace, zcontain, zmeat,
//                                         zturned), NO zm_octagonal
//
//  With the octagonal donor loaded early the build shipped Reimagined's rows
//  nowhere and octagonal's fine; with it at the tail, refreshed_donor won and
//  the built mod.ff came out with maxnum_map,7 and no octagonal row at all -
//  i.e. the Custom Maps route silently did not exist. Neither donor is the
//  answer: the file in zone_assets\zm\ is retail's table plus the zm_octagonal
//  rows, which is a strict superset of what the game uses today.
//
//  The five ZMUI_OCTAGONAL* refs those rows name are defined in
//  zone_assets\english\localizedstrings\mod.str - no fastfile anywhere defines
//  them, including the release's own.
stringtable,zm/gametypestable.csv
stringtable,zm/mapstable.csv

// The signpost pin on the globe.
image,menu_zm_map_signpost_octagonal
material,menu_zm_map_signpost_octagonal

// The map card in the Custom Maps list, its blurred transition copy, and the
// mode card. The four .iwi files that carry these pixels are tracked in
// images/ against the blanket images/*.iwi ignore - mod.ff holds only the
// image HEADERS, so a fresh checkout without them renders a placeholder.
image,menu_zm_map_octagonal
image,menu_zm_map_octagonal_blur
material,menu_zm_octagonal_map
material,menu_zm_octagonal_map_blur
image,menu_zm_map_octagonal_zclassic
material,menu_zm_octagonal_zclassic_octagonal

// The lobby's bottom-left preview panel. ui/t6/mapinfoimage.lua derives the
// name as "menu_" .. map .. "_" .. gamemode .. "_" .. location and folds every
// non-zclassic gametype to zsurvival, so the Custom Maps route (zstandard)
// asks for menu_zm_octagonal_zsurvival_octagonal. The pixels are the map card
// image above; the material is authored in zone_assets/materials/ on the
// menu_zm_transit_zsurvival_diner pattern.
material,menu_zm_octagonal_zsurvival_octagonal

// Loading screen, one material per gametype x start-location pair the engine
// can ask for. The engine builds the name from the dvars and falls back to a
// missing-material placeholder if the exact permutation is absent, so all
// eight stay.
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zstandard_zm_octagonal
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zclassic_zm_octagonal
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zstandard_
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zclassic_
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zclassic_mp_castaway
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zstandard_mp_castaway
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zclassic_octagonal
material,loadscreen_zm_octagonal_zstandard_octagonal

// 📝 NOT HERE ON PURPOSE: image/material overlay_low_health and image $white /
// material white. The donor declared them because a standalone mod.ff is the
// only file in its mod folder; common_zm.ff owns all four and loads on every
// map including this one, so declaring them here would only re-own a stock
// asset for no gain.
